question:
A boy collecting stamps was asked how many stamps he had in his album, to which he replied:

- If the number of stamps is divided by 2, the remainder is 1; 
- If divided by 3, the remainder is 2;
- If divided by 4, the remainder is 3;
- If divided by 5, the remainder is 4;
- If divided by 6, the remainder is 5;
- If divided by 7, the remainder is 6;
- If divided by 8, the remainder is 7;
- If divided by 9, the remainder is 8;
- If divided by 10, the remainder is 9.

The total number of stamps in the album is less than 3000.

How many stamps are in the album?

For all positive integers $n$ less than $2002$, let 
\begin{eqnarray*} a_n =\left\{ \begin{array}{lr} 11, & \text{if } n \text{ is divisible by } 13 \text{ and } 14;\\ 13, & \text{if } n \text{ is divisible by } 14 \text{ and } 11;\\ 14, & \text{if } n \text{ is divisible by } 11 \text{ and } 13;\\ 0, & \text{otherwise}. \end{array} \right. \end{eqnarray*}
Calculate $\sum_{n=1}^{2001} a_n$.

For all positive integers $n$ less than $2002$, let 
\begin{eqnarray*} a_n =\left\{ \begin{array}{lr} 11, & \text{if } n \text{ is divisible by } 13 \text{ and } 14;\\ 13, & \text{if } n \text{ is divisible by } 14 \text{ and } 11;\\ 14, & \text{if } n \text{ is divisible by } 11 \text{ and } 13;\\ 0, & \text{otherwise}. \end{array} \right. \end{eqnarray*}
Calculate $\sum_{n=1}^{2001} a_n$.

Given the function $f(x)=2\sqrt{2}\cos x\sin\left(x+\frac{\pi}{4}\right)-1$.  
(I) Find the value of $f\left(\frac{\pi}{4}\right)$;  
(II) Find the maximum and minimum values of $f(x)$ in the interval $\left[0, \frac{\pi}{2}\right]$.

In the figure below, the largest circle has a radius of six meters. Five congruent smaller circles are placed as shown and are lined up in east-to-west and north-to-south orientations. What is the radius in meters of one of the five smaller circles?

[asy]

size(3cm,3cm);

draw(Circle((0,0),1));

draw(Circle((0,2),1));

draw(Circle((0,-2),1));

draw(Circle((2,0),1));

draw(Circle((-2,0),1));

draw(Circle((0,0),3));

[/asy]

Solve the system of inequalities:

\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
|x-2a| \leq 3 \\
\log_{2}(x+a) \leq 2 
\end{array}
\right.
\]

which is equivalent to:

\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
-5 \leq x-2a \leq 5 \\
0 < x+a \leq 4 
\end{array}
\right.
\]

and further simplifies to:

\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
2a-5 \leq x \leq 2a+5 \\
-a < x \leq 4-a 
\end{array}
\right.
\]

The system has a unique solution if \(2a - 5 = 4 - a\), which gives \(a = 3\). In this case, the only solution for \(x\) is \(x = 1\).

